  annotation = {中文辅助译名：通过创新的多任务学习框架与基于融合模型的数据清理相集成，增强短期风电预测},
  abstract = {To enhance the training efficiency and prediction accuracy of multi-step short-term wind power prediction (WPP), and to tackle the challenge that data cleaning with only a single model fails to accurately detect complex outliers in wind power dataset, this study proposes a novel short-term WPP framework that integrates multi-task learning (MTL) with an advanced fusion data cleaning methodology (DCM). First, a hybrid machine learning model is designed for anomaly detection and correction. The Isolation Forest algorithm identifies global outliers in wind speed data, while a boundary-aware local density outlier detection algorithm captures local anomalies. Subsequently, the Density-Based Spatial Clustering of Applications with Noise algorithm uncovers abnormal wind speed-power generation relationships. Upon outlier detection, a backpropagation neural network performs anomaly correction, ensuring reconstructed data quality. The cleaned dataset then trains an MTL-based short-term multi-step WPP model. This framework partitions different time steps into distinct tasks and introduces Gaussian perturbations to historical power values during inter-task communication in training, mitigating discrepancies between training and prediction phases. A Decision Tree, Support Vector Machines and several shallow neural networks generate preliminary multi-step predictions, which are further refined by bidirectional long short-term memory (BiLSTM) network to produce final forecasts. Comprehensive},
}

