  annotation = {中文辅助译名：无人机视觉中使用多尺度特征和轻量级网络的电力线绝缘子小尺寸缺陷检测方法},
  abstract = {Insulator defect detection (IDD) of transmission lines is crucial for power system safety and stability, with Un-manned Aerial Vehicle (UAV)-based machine learning methods becoming prevalent. However, these methods face challenges due to deep neural networks’ high complexity/low detection speed and the difficulty in detecting small defects within complex UAV backgrounds. To address these issues, this article proposes a Multiscale Insulator Defect Detect Network (MID-Net) for IDD, comprising a fully connected GhostNet (FCG-Net) backbone, a generalized multiscale spatial convolution (GMSC) module, and a category prediction head (CPH) module. First, the lightweight FCG-Net backbone network is designed to reduce the network’s computational cost. Second, the GMSC module enhances small defect feature representation and enables interactive multiscale feature fusion. Finally, the Focal-EIOU loss in the CPH module improves model convergence and robustness. Experimental findings demonstrate the proposed approach’s effectiveness in both detection accuracy and efficiency.},
}

@misc{badong_chen_5909ba3a0a2aa9c5,
